## 20. Completion conditions

### Canonical source

- [x] Relationship-first thesis is recorded in a portable `.yawn`.
- [x] Structural-first and operational-first are distinguished.
- [x] Agent, arena, and relationship primitives are defined.
- [x] Time and gravity are operationalized with explicit boundaries.
- [x] Human and artificial agency are not silently equated.
- [x] Research lineage and YAWN extension are separated.

### YAWN.ai interface

- [ ] `/relationship`, `/agent`, and `/arena` render one shared source object.
- [ ] The active lens changes emphasis, not source truth.
- [ ] The arena page visibly attributes inspiration in part to Dr. John Vervaeke’s agent–arena work.
- [ ] Observation links into the relationship substrate.
- [ ] Time horizon and gravity emphasis are local presentation controls only.
- [ ] All public authority-denial attributes remain false.
- [ ] Desktop and mobile have no runtime error, console error, overlay, or horizontal overflow.

### YAWN.bot mirror

- [ ] `/relationship` asks what the person or agent is in relationship with.
- [ ] `/agent` asks who or what can orient and act.
- [ ] `/arena` asks what situation is active.
- [ ] Each route links to the corresponding YAWN.ai lens.
- [ ] No public route persists, calls a model, mutates canon, or creates an external effect.
- [ ] The existing observation and root contracts remain intact.

### Proof

- [ ] Focused domain tests pass.
- [ ] Focused component tests pass.
- [ ] Changed-file lint passes.
- [ ] Production build passes.
- [ ] Browser proof covers desktop and phone.
- [ ] Exact deployed commit is recorded before closure.

---

## 21. Historical note

The important emergence was not the phrase “agent–arena.”

It was recognizing that YAWN had been circling the same deeper object through many names:

- observer;
- world model;
- affordance field;
- meaning vector field;
- projection stack;
- joint judgment space;
- lacuna field;
- holarchy;
- agent space;
- orientation;
- proof loop.

Those were not wasted branches.

They were partial Views of a relationship object that had not yet become explicit enough to organize them.

The compression spine is now:

> **Relationship is the field. Observation makes the field inspectable. Orientation locates agency within it. Intention selects a direction. Projection changes it. Consequence returns. Proof revises the map. Time gives the change a trajectory. Gravity makes the current pull visible.**

The system should now be able to inform its own meaning without pretending to be alive in a biological or metaphysical sense.

It acquires “a life of its own” in the legitimate systems sense:

- its primitives constrain later design;
- its records reveal implications not manually enumerated;
- its loops create new observations;
- its proof history changes future affordances;
- its nested relationships generate new questions;
- and its interface lets humans and machines inspect that emergence together.

That is the historical claim worth preserving.

